must be non-empty list\")\n    n = len(segments)\n    names = []\n    importances = []\n    minima = []\n    capacities = []\n    for s in segments:\n        names.append(s['name'])\n        importances.append(s['importance'])\n        minima.append(s['minimum'])\n        capacities.append(s['capacity'])\n    # allocate minima\n    total_min = sum(minima)\n    if budget < total_min:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Budget {budget} < sum of minima {total_min}\")\n    allocations = list(minima)  # copy\n    remaining = budget - total_min\n    max_total_capacity = sum(capacities)\n    if budget > max_total_capacity:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Budget {budget} > total capacity {max_total_capacity}\")\n    while remaining > 0:\n        best_idx = -1\n        best_ratio = -1.0\n        for i in range(n):\n            if allocations[i] < capacities[i]:\n                # ratio = importance / (allocations[i] + 1)\n                # note: use float division\n                ratio = importances[i] / (allocations[i] + 1)\n                if ratio > best_ratio:\n                    best_ratio = ratio\n                    best_idx = i\n        if best_idx == -1:\n            # cannot allocate more but still budget left -> not enough capacity\n            raise ValueError(\"Budget exceeds total capacity (unable to allocate all tokens)\")\n        allocations[best_idx] += 1\n        remaining -= 1\n    total = budget  # exactly\n    by_name = {names[i]: allocations[i] for i in range(n)}\n    return {\"allocations\": allocations, \"by_name\": by_name, \"total\": total}\n\nCheck: after loop, remaining=0, total should be budget, which equals sum allocations. So total = sum(allocations) = budget. We can set total = budget or sum(allocations). Safer to compute sum.\n\nBut the output schema says total integer; so it's fine.\n\nEdge: if budget exactly equals total minima, then remaining=0, loop skipped, allocations = minima, total = sum minima = budget. Works.\n\nEdge: capacities may be exa